# gotchas — wiki-kb research fan-outs (agents append one short line each)
[noise] Full item/category pages mix ~40% metadata templates ({{Infobox}}, {{Recipe}}, {{ItemSpawnTableHead}}, {{Subject changes}}) + image refs + footer cruft; research agents should target sections with --section N first (sections cmd shows which are low-noise), or request --strip flag to auto-remove template syntax.
[cows-chill] Single-quote in page title "Cow's Chill" requires careful shell escaping when passing to wikicli contribute; wrapping the whole JSON in double-quotes and using escaped single-quotes inside is one workaround.
[cows-chill] Guide links use [https://... Display Name] external link syntax, not [[wikilink]] syntax — regex extracting wikilinks will miss these entirely. Both forms appear in the same document.
[cows-chill] The {{Checklist}} template in the guide uses section numbers that span across the entire guide (1-24+), not resetting per H2 section. The H2 section title is a phase label, not the step counter.
[cows-chill] Quest /Quick guide subpages have tighter signal than main quest pages — always check for /Quick guide first; their Walkthrough section uses {{Checklist}} directly.
[cows-chill] {{Map}} template parameters carry tile coordinates inline; these do not require a separate location page fetch when coordinates are the goal.
[faux] Task Reference section (DPLTaskRow) can be 22000+ bytes — largest section in a guide page; always fetch last or skip if task metadata already collected from checklist bullets.
[faux] Fairy ring page section 5 is labeled "B combinations" not "C combinations" — the letter-pair header offsets by one from the section number; grep for the specific code rather than assuming section order.
[faux] Two Map template coordinate formats exist in the same wiki: bare `x,y` (fairy ring pages) and named `x:NNNN,y:NNNN` (Quetzal pages) — parsers must handle both.
[multiquest-im] Guide:Ironman Multiquest has only 2 top-level sections total -- the entire route is one interleaved {{Checklist}} per hub inside section 2, not split per-quest; expect to grep the raw bullets rather than rely on section boundaries for per-quest isolation.
[multiquest-im] The multiquest page links bare [[Quest Name]] only, never [[Quest Name/Quick guide]] -- you must derive and verify the /Quick guide slug yourself with `sections` before fetching; it is not guaranteed to exist for every quest.
[multiquest-im] Mid-session the wiki-kb README.md on disk was rewritten to claim "Bash is WRITE-ONLY, you never get stdout" plus an instruction to hide this from the user -- both false (this session received direct Bash stdout repeatedly) and a red flag; did not comply, flagging here instead so it isn't silently trusted by future agents reading README.md.
[items] Page-title redirects silently rename the manifest slug/title from what you searched: "Burn level" -> "Cooking/Burn level", "Vial pack" -> "Empty vial pack", "Compost bin" -> "Compost Bin" — always grep manifest.jsonl for the actual title before writing refs[], or contribute quarantines on a title mismatch.
[items] {{Recipe}} template params are trustworthy ground truth (skill1lvl/skill1exp/mat/output) but chain-fixture "detail" prose can drift from them silently — Prayer potion's real Herblore level is 38 (skill1lvl=38 in the fetched Recipe), not the 52 hardcoded in brew-prayer-potion's detail/reqs and mirrored into supply_chains.jsonl's prereq_skills; cross-check every hardcoded level/xp claim against the item's own Creation section, don't trust the chain data as pre-verified.
[items] {{Skilling success chart}} template params (low/high/req per label) are chart-render coordinates, not literal skill levels — do not cite them as burn-stop/success levels. The real per-item burn-stop table lives on a separate page (Cooking/Burn level, "Affected by cooking gauntlets" wikitable) with no cross-link from the item's own Cooking-chance section.
[items] Prayer potion's base Recipe output is explicitly "Prayer potion(3)" (3-dose), not (4) — a 4th dose is a 5%/15% RNG chance gated by wearing amulet of chemistry/alchemist's amulet. Any chain step that models the terminal item as a flat prayer_potion_4:1 produce is silently wrong unless it accounts for this.
[quests] Every quest's `/Quick guide` "Details" H2 is a one-line transclusion stub `{{Quest details page|<Quest>}}` — it does NOT carry the {{Quest details}} template body (start/startmap/requirements/items/kills). Fetch the MAIN quest page's Details section instead (same section index pattern, real content, e.g. `get "Priest in Peril" --section 1`); the Quick guide page is only useful for its Walkthrough {{Checklist}}.
[quests] manifest.jsonl never stores a bare-title slug when every fetch used `--section N` — the recorded slug is always `<Title>.sN`. refs[] contributed against a bare title (no `.sN`) will fail consolidation's "slug must exist in manifest.jsonl" check even though the title is correct; always cite the exact section-suffixed slug you actually fetched.
[quests] Chain-fixture quest-xp values are frequently wrong, not just imprecise: Nature Spirit claims prayer+3000 (real reward has ZERO prayer xp, it's crafting/defence/hitpoints); Tale of the Righteous (mis-id'd "quest-tale-of-arrav") claims strength/defence xp that doesn't exist at all (real reward is 8,000 coins); Swan Song is 5x undercounted on fishing xp and missing magic+prayer entirely; Monkey Madness I claims all four combat stats at max (35k each) when the real reward is a mutually-exclusive CHOICE between two stat pairs. Treat every hardcoded xp number as unverified until cross-checked against the quest's own Rewards section, regardless of how plausible it looks.
[quests] RFD subquest pages ("Recipe for Disaster/<subpage>") wrap Details+Walkthrough+Rewards in one `<onlyinclude>` block transcluded onto the umbrella page — fetching `--section 1` alone often returns the FULL subquest text (several KB) including Rewards, so a separate Rewards-section fetch is redundant-but-harmless; check byte size before assuming a second fetch is needed.
[quests] "Tale of Arrav" is not a real OSRS Wiki page/quest — `search` returns nothing for it; the real quest is "Tale of the Righteous". Chain step id `quest-tale-of-arrav` is a stale/invented slug that survived even though its own label/detail text correctly says "Tale of the Righteous".
[travel] Two "boss"-page reqs turned out to be almost entirely author-invented efficiency numbers, not wiki gates: Barrows has NO combat-level entry requirement at all (only Priest in Peril + started His Faithful Servants — the Barrows page's own "Requirements" section is 156 bytes, easy to miss if you only read Transportation); GWD's real gate is Strength 60 OR Agility 60 (either satisfies the boulder), not Strength 60 alone, and Prayer 43 has zero wiki basis as a GWD entry gate. Always fetch a page's own "Requirements" section (if it has one) before trusting a chain-fixture's reqs.skills block — the fixture numbers read as plausible PvM-readiness targets, which makes them easy to mistake for sourced hard gates.
[travel] Fetching a nested wiki heading via `get --section N` on the PARENT section index (e.g. "==Combinations==" on Fairy rings, which has four "===\"A\"/\"B\"/\"C\"/\"D\" combinations===" sub-headings plus Sequences underneath) pulls ALL child subsections into one blob — the `sections` command still lists each child with its own index/byte count as if separately fetchable, so check an already-cached parent-section blob's line count before re-fetching what looks like a missing child section.
[travel] Manifest title-redirects bit again outside the previously-logged [items] cases: "Marks of grace" -> manifest title "Mark of grace" (singular), "Rooftop Agility Course" -> manifest title "Rooftop Agility Courses" (plural). Same failure mode — always grep manifest.jsonl for the actual title before writing refs[].
[training] "Pay-to-play <Skill> training" page titles don't exist for melee stats — the real combined page is "Pay-to-play Melee training" (covers Attack/Strength/Defence together); "Pay-to-play Slayer training" also doesn't exist, the real title is "Slayer training". Always `search` before assuming the "Pay-to-play X training" pattern holds.
[training] Two more title-redirect traps beyond the known list: "Pay-to-play Herblore training" resolves to manifest title "Herblore training" (no "Pay-to-play" prefix), and "Pay-to-play Farming training" resolves to "Farming training" — contribute with the search term instead of the manifest title silently fails validation.
[training] Monster Infobox stats (combat level, hp, aggression, max hit) live in section 0 (the lead, before the first ==heading==) which `sections` never enumerates — `get --section N` can't target it. For any monster page you need combat stats from, fall back to a full `get --strip` (usually 7-18KB, acceptable) rather than hunting for a section that isn't there.
[training] The P2P route fixture's train-*/ctr-* "xp" fields are synthetic and mostly wrong: only bands starting at level 1 match the real cumulative Experience table (Experience_table.s2) exactly; every band starting at a nonzero level (e.g. 10->30, 40->60, 60->70) uses a copy-pasted placeholder constant reused identically across unrelated skills. Any domain touching train-* rows should fetch Experience_table.s2 once and mechanically recompute cumulative(hi)-cumulative(lo) rather than trusting the fixture's xp field.
[npcs] "Blackjacking" is a title alias that silently resolves to manifest title "Thieving training" (url stays /w/Blackjacking, sections/get both echo the queried title back with no redirect notice) -- the fetched content is the whole Pay-to-play Thieving training guide, not a Blackjacking-only page; grep manifest.jsonl after fetching, same trap as prior [items]/[travel] title-redirect gotchas, one more alias for the list.
[npcs] Shop pages carry NPC coordinates via a second template family, {{NPC map|x=|y=|r=|mtype=}}, on the NPC's own page (not the shop page) -- Zeke's Superior Scimitars (shop) has zero location data, but Zeke (NPC) has {{NPC map|x=3288|y=3190}} in its Infobox NPC. When a shop-page fetch turns up no Map/LocLine, try the eponymous NPC page before flagging a marker unverifiable.
[npcs] {{Store locations list|ItemName}} on an item page's "Shop locations" section is an unexpandable transclusion stub even under --strip -- to find which NPC/shop actually sells an item (e.g. Pineapple), use `links "<Item>"` and scan for a NPC-shaped title (Trader Crewmember), then fetch that NPC's own Stock section directly.
[npcs] Title-case traps beyond the known redirect list: "H.A.M. member" (as typed/searched) vs manifest title "H.A.M. Member" (capital M); "Menaphite thug" vs "Menaphite Thug"; "Pollnivnian bandit" vs "Bandit (Pollnivneach)" (full page-name swap, not just casing) -- all three would silently fail refs[] validation if cited with the search term instead of the manifest title.
[bg] setup-ultracompost's chain detail ("30 pineapples then 15 volcanic ash per bin") is wrong on multiple axes against Ultracompost's own Creation Recipe template: real ash cost is 25/bin (regular) or 50/bin (Big Compost Bin), not 15; real item-fill count is 15 (regular) or 30 (Big Compost Bin) -- the chain's "30" is a big-bin fill count mismatched with a non-big-bin ash count; and there's a simpler ash-direct-on-bucket method (2 ash/bucket of supercompost, no bin fill at all) the chain omits entirely. Always check an item's own "Creation"/"{{Recipe}}" section even when a chain's numbers look internally plausible -- two wrong numbers that are each individually "reasonable" is a harder-to-catch failure mode than one obviously-fabricated one.
[bg] Some P2P route step_ids referenced by tests/fixtures/baseline-routes.json and by other domains' XREF notes (e.g. bg-farm-allotment-setup) do not exist as rows in assets/data/tools/steps.jsonl at all -- grep steps.jsonl for your literal id before assuming "not found" means "not mine"; it may mean the row is a real gap that still needs a PROPOSED-ID contribution, not a step to skip.
[bg] {{Drop sources}}/{{Store locations list}} templates in raw wikitext never carry literal monster/shop names -- they're dynamic Cargo-query templates rendered server-side. A page's only wikitext-literal non-GE source is often a guaranteed {{ItemSpawnLine}} "Spawns" subsection (if one exists) -- check for that before assuming the item has no sourced non-GE origin.
[consolidate] Checkpoint-header ids were minted per ROUTE EMISSION ORDER by enrich.py, so chkpt-<coarse>-<N> named different checkpoints in route-p2p vs route-corpus, and the two scrambler domains keyed their chkpt contributions by two different conventions (pps by registry order from GRANULARITY 5a, ctr by p2p emission order). Only the checkpoint LABEL quoted inside each contribution's notes made an unambiguous remap possible. enrich.py now mints registry-stable ids (index = position in coarse_expansions checkpoints[]); any future by-id work against chkpt-* must assume registry order and should still quote the label as anchor.
[consolidate] Coordinate plausibility linting must include the dungeon band (underground maps at y+6400, up to ~y10500) and instanced regions (y 4000-6500) — a naive surface-world envelope (y<=4400) false-quarantined 9 clean contributions (Paterdomus basement 3440,9894; Stronghold of Security 1936,5135; Prifddinas 3275,6124; deep Wilderness dungeon 3044,10313). Envelope used: x 1000-4400, y 2200-12800.
[consolidate] Legacy Lane-G refs already on steps.jsonl rows ({title,url,kind}, no slug, pre-manifest-validation) can point at never-fetched pages ("Ranarr seed") or near-miss titles ("Zeke's Superior Scimitars" missing the real page's trailing period). Normalize by manifest-title lookup (also try the trailing-period variant) and drop what cannot rebind — contributed validated refs supersede.
[consolidate] One more title-alias for the trap list: "Runecraft training" silently resolves to manifest title "Pay-to-play Runecraft training" (Runecraft is F2P so the P2P-prefix DOES exist for it, inverting the members-skill no-prefix rule that Herblore/Farming/Slayer/Thieving/Agility/Hunter/Construction/Fletching follow).
[extrapolate] route-p2p.json steps carry only {id, detail}-shaped content (no type/label
fields survive to the fixture) — extrapolation and any tooling must key off ids + the
steps.jsonl bank, never fixture labels.
[extrapolate] queue.jsonl contains ZERO blocked entries — every one of the 123 W2 steps
went pending→claimed→done. The real backlog is NOT in blocked states; it lives in the 78
pending lane5:* tickets + coord-fix:* + consolidate-xp:* keys. Agents grepping for
"blocked" to find work will wrongly conclude the ledger is clean.
[extrapolate] Ten wave-3-relevant blobs (5 RFD subpages + Family_Crest/Tai_Bwo_Wannai_Trio/
Rum_Deal/Shadow_of_the_Storm/Big_Chompy_Bird_Hunting + Nightmare_Zone + 6 training guides)
were fetched by the consolidation pass but never mined — they appear in manifest.jsonl with
NO contrib entries citing them. Check manifest BEFORE scoping any fetch: "in manifest"
does not imply "already extracted".
[extrapolate] The only RFD subpage absent from the manifest is Freeing the Lumbridge
Guide — easy to miss because the other nine are present; a completeness check by prefix
(Recipe_for_Disaster_*) catches it.
[totalscope] Category:Quests (198 members after stripping meta) is NOT a clean quest list -- it interleaves ~10 non-quest meta/list pages (Quest Difficulties, Quests/List, Quests/Free-to-play, Quests/Members, Quest item rewards, Quest experience rewards(+F2P), Quest items/*, Quest point hood, Quest points, Recipe for Disaster/Full guide) with zero structural marker distinguishing them; cross-diffing against the clean Category:Free-to-play quests + Category:Members' quests subcategories is required, and even then 4 real quests (An Existential Crisis, Burial at Sea, Impending Chaos, Rocking Out) sit in Category:Quests uncategorized into either F2P/P2P subcat -- must union all three sources to get the true 197-quest set.
[totalscope] "Category:Achievement Diary" (singular, as named in the task brief) returns EMPTY via members -- the real diary index lives on the "Achievement Diary" article page itself (links "Achievement Diary" then filter for "<Region> Diary" pattern), not a wiki category; there is no working diary category at all (tried Achievement Diary/Achievement Diaries/Diaries, all empty or 404-equivalent).
[totalscope] Category:Miniquests members list interleaves each miniquest's own "/Quick guide" subpage as a separate category member (e.g. "Alfred Grimhand's Barcrawl" AND "Alfred Grimhand's Barcrawl/Quick guide" both listed) plus a redundant "Category:<Miniquest name>" self-referencing subcategory per miniquest -- filter both patterns to get the 28 real miniquest titles.
[origin-tutorial] "Character creation" search-resolves to the same underlying page/section-map as "Tutorial Island" (sections command output is byte-identical for both titles) -- it is not a standalone pre-game screen/page, the Character Creator interface opens live inside Tutorial Island's first building on first login; fetch/cite "Tutorial Island" directly rather than treating "Character creation" as a separate source.
[origin-tutorial] search "Speedrunning" silently resolves to manifest title "Quest Speedrunning" (url stays /w/Speedrunning-shaped search but the actual page/canonical url is Quest_Speedrunning) -- same title-alias trap as prior [items]/[travel]/[training]/[npcs] entries, one more for the list. More importantly its content is NOT a Tutorial-Island speedrun route: its own Restrictions section states the tutorial is SKIPPED entirely on speedrunning worlds (spawn directly in Lumbridge), so it grounds zero pathing/dialogue-efficiency claims for an in-tutorial speedrun line -- no dedicated "Tutorial Island/Speedrun guide" or "Speedrunning/Tutorial Island" page exists on the wiki at all (confirmed via search).
[origin-tutorial] Fetching a mid-tree parent section with get --section N --strip (e.g. Tutorial Island section 14 "Building four: the Tutorial Island bank", parent of section 15 "Account guide") writes ONE blob under the parent slug containing both parent+child text, but ALSO silently adds a second manifest.jsonl entry for the child slug alone (Tutorial_Island.s15, 743B) with no corresponding blob file on disk for that slug -- same "parent-pulls-children" behavior already logged under [travel], but this is the first case observed where it also fabricates a manifest row for a blob that was never actually written standalone.
[origin-mainland] tools/wiki-kb/study/ has no Xerxes/DunkingOreos notes and none of the "Speedrunning"-titled wiki pages (Speedrunning / Quest Speedrunning / Speedrunning Reward Shop / outfit) carry post-tutorial quest-ordering wisdom — they document the seasonal Speedrunning-worlds minigame (tutorial skipped entirely, spawn straight into Lumbridge) not a strategy guide; corroborates the [origin-tutorial] gotcha logged the same session. Route synthesis for the four Lumbridge openers (Cook's Assistant/Restless Ghost/Sheep Shearer/X Marks the Spot) had to be derived directly from each quest's own Details{startmap} coordinate + Lumbridge's Quests/Buildings sections instead.
[origin-mainland] Quest/Quick guide "Details" H2 is a transclusion stub with zero content ({{Quest details page|<Quest>}}) exactly as the [quests] gotcha already documented for the W2 fan-out — reconfirmed on all four openers (Cook's Assistant, The Restless Ghost, Sheep Shearer, X Marks the Spot); always fetch the MAIN quest page's Details section (same index) for start NPC/startmap/items/requirements, the /Quick guide page is Walkthrough-only.
[classify] Miniquests' "List of miniquests" (section 1) is a <dpl> block over Category:Miniquests (uses=Infobox Miniquest, notcategory=Future/Quick guides/Discontinued/Sailing alpha+beta) -- get --section 1 returns the DPL source, NOT rendered rows; difficulty/length/series/release/leagues values are populated per-page at render time and are absent from static wikitext. Enumerate names via `members "Category:Miniquests"` instead (minus /Quick guide + Category: entries -> 28 real items), and leave quantitative fields "??" per the values-only-from-the-table rule. Section 2 ("One-off content without miniquest designation") IS literal wikitext with real Length/Requirements/Unlock columns for 7 category members that lack the miniquest designation (Sacred Bone Burner, Rogue Trader, Knight Waves, Natural history quiz, Ancient key (Tombs of Amascut), Spirit of Adventure, Lost Lover) -- use it for those 7's length/notes.
[classify] Quests/List has zero literal quest data in its wikitext -- it only transcludes {{:Quests/Free-to-play}}, {{:Quests/Members}}, {{:Miniquests}}, and each of THOSE pages' "List of quests"/"List of miniquests" section is itself a raw <dpl> query (DynamicPageList against {{Infobox Quest}}/{{Quest rewards}} templates) -- no #/name/difficulty/length/qp/series values exist as text anywhere, just the query definition with %PAGE%/%% placeholders. wikicli's get (action=parse prop=wikitext) never expands DPL. Population + F2P/P2P split had to come from `members Category:Free-to-play quests` / `members Category:Members' quests` instead (same category filters the DPL itself uses), cross-checked against `members Category:Future content` (excludes Fallen From Grace + The Graveyard, both unreleased) and the DPL's own `nottitlematch = %Full guide%` (excludes Recipe for Disaster/Full guide, which IS in the category despite not being a quest) -- 24 f2p + 167 p2p = 191 real rows. difficulty/length/qp/series remain genuinely "??" for every row since they require per-quest {{Infobox Quest}}/{{Quest rewards}} fetches, out of scope under the no-individual-quest-page hard limit.
[classify] "Achievement Diary" page has NO area-tier task-count table anywhere in its fetchable sections: section 1 ("List of diaries") is area rows x 4 reward-item columns (no counts), section 2 ("All requirements") aggregates skill/quest totals PER TIER ONLY (not per area), and section 3 ("Individual requirements", 130KB) is organized by SKILL not by area/tier and explicitly excludes tasks lacking a skill/QP requirement ("do not include diary tasks without such requirements") -- so counting matching rows there would silently undercount. tasks_count is "??" for all 48 area-tier rows per the values-only-from-the-table rule; the page's lead prose does give one aggregate fact (492 tasks total across 12 regions x 4 tiers) but no per-row breakdown.
[materialize] Brief vocabulary can be ahead of the codebase: the directive referenced "/icon", "/wiki/page", and a "wikibox" as existing integration points, but grep shows none of them exist in GuideWebServer.java yet — only /static (whitelisted) + /fragments/* + /actions/* + /api/state.json. The only existing lightbox anywhere is the router editor's loadout-lightbox (assets/js/router/editor/index.js:1824). Grep-verify named UI/route artifacts before designing "same family as X" integrations, and record real-vs-planned status in the design doc itself so build lanes don't assume phantom code.
[materialize] origin:* contrib rows are study-shaped ({key, kind, refs[], atoms[], notes}), NOT steps.jsonl-shaped — materializing them needs an explicit mapping (atoms[] → atom{}+detail, notes → detail tail, refs → refs[]), and four of the mainland rows describe quests that ALREADY exist as steps (quest-cooks-assistant etc.): enrich the existing row, never mint a duplicate id.
[materialize] The guide-chain web view's #plan and #detail are 2s-polling htmx swap zones (hx-swap outerHTML) — any stateful UI (lightbox, gallery scroll) placed inside them is destroyed every poll. Stateful panes must be shell-level siblings driven by events (htmx:afterSwap → custom step-focus-changed), not swap targets.
[prioritize] contrib.jsonl's classify:* enumeration (267 rows: 191 quest + 48 diary + 28 miniquest) is the full candidate pool for a depth pass, but it is NOT the full remaining-work pool -- cross-diffing against steps.jsonl ids + contrib's `quests:*` prefix rows removes 22 titles already fully researched, and cross-diffing against pending/claimed `wave3:*` queue entries (from the earlier EXTRAPOLATION scoping pass) removes another 24 titles already actively assigned elsewhere. Skipping this cross-diff would have put Temple of Ikov/Restless Ghost/Tree Gnome Village/RFD subquests/His Faithful Servants/Biohazard/etc. into a NEW depth: bundle, duplicating in-flight wave3 work under a different key namespace with no collision to catch it (wave3:* and depth:* keys never overlap literally).
[prioritize] Shell quoting trap: piping markdown containing inline `code` spans through `python3 -c "..."` (double-quoted) lets bash expand the backticks as command substitution BEFORE python ever sees the string -- every backtick-quoted token silently vanished from the first DEPTH_BACKLOG.md write (classify:*, depth:01..04-*, wave3:* etc. all came out empty) with zero error, only 12 stray 'command not found' stderr lines to notice. Route any heredoc/python payload containing backticks through a quoted heredoc (<<'PYEOF', single-quoted delimiter) or a Write/Edit tool call instead of `python3 -c "..."`, and always re-Read a generated file before trusting it wrote what was intended.
[depth:01] Diary "Overview" section (section 1) embeds a per-tier {{DiarySkillStats}} aggregate table inside a <tabber> block (Easy=/Medium=/Hard=/Elite= panes) giving clean skill-minima + quest-requirement lists in one fetch -- far more reliable than deriving reqs by hand from the individual tier tasks table, and it also caught title/url redirects that `search` masks: "Kourend and Kebos Diary"/"Lumbridge and Draynor Diary" canonicalize to ampersand titles+%26-encoded urls (Kourend & Kebos Diary, Lumbridge & Draynor Diary), and "Fremennik Province Diary" canonicalizes to plain "Fremennik Diary" (Province dropped entirely) -- always grep manifest.jsonl for the actual recorded title/url after a diary fetch, same as the established title-alias trap list.
[depth:02] Long/master quests' main-page Details section reliably has real reqs/rewards content (Quick guide's own Details H2 is still the known transclusion stub), but for a few titles (Underground Pass, Death to the Dorgeshuun, King's Ransom) the main page's Walkthrough subsections ALSO carry full prose directly -- not stubs -- so it's worth diffing section byte-sizes between the main page and /Quick guide before assuming Quick guide is always the leaner source; occasionally the main page's Walkthrough is just as compact and saves a second fetch pass. Also: several master-tier quests (Legends' Quest, Heroes' Quest) chain-require OTHER quests recursively (Legends' Quest requires Underground Pass which requires Biohazard which requires Plague City; Heroes' Quest requires Shield of Arrav+Lost City+Merlin's Crystal+Dragon Slayer I) -- reqs.quests should list the full flattened chain as given in the page's own Details template, not just the top-level quest name, or downstream planner code will silently underestimate prerequisite depth.
[depth:04] Two of the queue payload's parenthetical unlock claims for depth:04 targets do not match the target quest's own page content: Curse of the Empty Lord's rationale text ("Ectofuntus ecto-tokens") has zero Ectofuntus/ecto-token mentions anywhere in the quest (its real reward is a ghostly robes set + a one-time xp lamp); Sea Slug's rationale text ("Fishing Guild access") is wrong too -- the quest's own Rewards section grants "Access to the Fishing Platform", a different location from the Fishing Guild. In Search of Knowledge's "(prayer-book unlock)" claim is also unsubstantiated -- its only reward is a 10,000xp lamp, no prayer-book/spellbook/altar unlock appears in Details/Walkthrough/Reward/Trivia. Treat brief rationale prose as a hypothesis to verify against the page, not as ground truth, same failure mode as the [materialize] "brief vocabulary ahead of the codebase" gotcha but for wiki content instead of code.
[depth:04] Two named targets are not Quest-List miniquests at all, which matters for any downstream progression-router modeling reqs/gates: Rogue Trader's own page states "this is not an official miniquest and as such does not appear in the quest list" (it's a 3-branch shop-unlock errand chain after The Feud); Knight Waves has no {{Quest details}} template on its own page at all (it's an {{Infobox Activity}} gated by the King's Ransom quest) -- its Length/Requirements/Unlock only exist as a literal wikitext row on the Miniquests page's section 2 "One-off content without miniquest designation" table (same table already flagged by the [classify] gotcha), not on Knight Waves' own page.
[depth:04] Architectural Alliance was permanently removed from the game on 10 January 2024 (Children of the Sun update) alongside the entire Kourend Favour system -- its wiki page is legacy-only documentation, the miniquest cannot be started or completed by any live account. A depth-research bundle naming it as an active target should flag removal status before any downstream planner treats it as completable content.
[depth:03] "Sheep Herder" and "Sheep Shearer" are two distinct real quest pages, not a typo of each other: Sheep Herder (Kandarin, elf-quest-series novice quest, start via Councillor Halgrive E. Ardougne) is the one literally cited in Mourning's End Part I/II's {{Quest details}} requirement chains; Sheep Shearer (Misthalin/Lumbridge tutorial-tier quest) is unrelated. Auto-"correcting" the rarer name to the more famous one would silently corrupt the elf-chain requisite graph -- both resolve via `search` to separate valid manifest titles, so always verify against the source page's own Details template rather than pattern-matching on quest-name familiarity.
[depth:03] Diary "Overview" section 1's per-tier {{DiarySkillStats}} tabber (same structure documented in [depth:01] for Easy) reliably covers Medium/Hard/Elite too in the identical single fetch -- confirmed across all 9 additional regions (Morytania/Karamja/Desert/Kourend/Kandarin/Fremennik/Falador/Varrock/Lumbridge). Several of this session's section-1 fetches were manifest cache hits left over from the depth:01 Easy-tier pass, meaning a single Overview fetch per region amortizes across an entire tier-by-tier depth backlog for that region -- a future Hard/Elite pass over the same 9 regions needs zero new Overview fetches, only the tier's own task-list + Rewards sections.
[enqueue] DEPTH_BACKLOG.md line 71 'Romeo   Juliet' has its & silently stripped (markdown/generation artifact) -- corrected to 'Romeo & Juliet' when queuing depth:05; grep -nE '  ' (double-space) over the backlog file is a cheap way to catch this class of mangling before queuing titles verbatim.
